cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "relu-sat-bench: provably hard neural network verification instances with known answers, generated from SAT"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Adrian
    family-names: Wurm
    affiliation: "Brandenburg University of Technology Cottbus-Senftenberg"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0481-9223"
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24417857  # all versions; version 1.0.0: 10.5281/zenodo.24417858
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/adrianwurm/relu-sat-bench"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for neural network verifiers built from a reduction of SAT to ReLU network verification:
  every instance is a ReLU network, the input box [0, 1]^n and a property that is violated if and only if
  the underlying CNF formula is satisfiable. Answers are known from a SAT solver or from the construction,
  and the difficulty follows the formula (random 3-SAT around the phase transition, planted solutions,
  pigeonhole, Tseitin and ordering formulas). The repository contains the generator, the export to ONNX
  and VNN-LIB, Docker setups for alpha,beta-CROWN and Marabou, the result files of all runs and their
  evaluation. Code under MIT, benchmark data under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - neural network verification
  - benchmark
  - SAT
  - ReLU networks
  - VNN-COMP
